  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Sophia Martin, and she wants to change the address for an order and her default address, then exchange a tablet. First, I need to authenticate her. The email was used to find her user ID, which is sophia_martin_8570. Now, I should get her user details to confirm the current default address and check her orders.\n\nNext, she mentioned changing the wrong order address to the new home. Since she doesn't want to reveal her address, I need to look up the orders associated with her user ID. The order for the tablet was sent to the old address, so I need to modify that order's shipping address. Also, she wants to update her default address. \n\nAfter handling the address changes, she wants to exchange the tablet for the cheapest one. I'll need to check the product details for tablets to find the cheapest variant. Then, use the exchange function for delivered orders. But wait, the order status needs to be checked. If the tablet order is delivered, exchange is possible. If pending, maybe modify items. But she mentioned moving costs, so exchange is the way to go.\n\nI should proceed step by step: get user details, then modify default address, modify order address, check order status, and then handle the exchange. Each step requires user confirmation. Let's start with getting her user details to see current info.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"sophia_martin_8570\"}}\n",
